<?php declare(strict_types=1); ?><!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0"><meta name="description" content="Project Unveiled presents Truth on Trial, powered by the Trust-Worthy investigation method. Question everything, inspect the evidence, and you be the judge."><title>Project Unveiled | Truth on Trial</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/truth/truth-worthy.css"></head><body><header class="topbar"><div class="wrap nav"><a class="brand" href="/truth/">PROJECT UNVEILED <span>TRUTH ON TRIAL</span></a><nav class="navlinks"><a href="#featured">Featured Trial</a><a href="#trials">Truth Trials</a><a href="#ask">Ask a Question</a><a href="/book/research.html">Research Standards</a></nav></div></header><main><section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">PROJECT UNVEILED · TRUTH ON TRIAL · POWERED BY TRUST-WORTHY</div><h1>QUESTION EVERYTHING!</h1><p>Bring the question. We trace the evidence, test the strongest competing explanations, expose what does not add up, and separate what is proven from what is inferred or still unknown.</p><div class="manifesto"><strong>We do not tell you what to think.</strong> We show our work. <strong>You be the judge.</strong></div></div></section><section class="section" id="featured"><div class="wrap"><article class="card daily-desk"><div class="eyebrow">FLAGSHIP TRUTH TRIAL · CASE 000003</div><h2>Who was Jesus — before religion told us who he was?</h2><p>Not “What does Christianity say?” This trial separates the earliest recoverable evidence about Jesus from later tradition, theological interpretation, skeptical assumptions, and claims that history alone cannot prove.</p><div class="finding"><strong>Free finding:</strong> The surviving early evidence supports a historical first-century Jesus behind the Christian movement. That historical core does not automatically prove every later theological claim—or disprove the extraordinary claims his earliest followers made about him.</div><p><a class="button" href="/truth/case-000003.php">Put Jesus on Trial</a></p></article></div></section><section class="section" id="trials"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Published & Open Investigations</div><h2>Truth Trials</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><div class="case-head"><div><div class="case-id">TW-CLAIM-000001</div><h2>Does God individually cause or permit every bad thing?</h2></div><div class="status">PROVISIONAL</div></div><p>The evidence does not require the conclusion that every harmful event is individually caused or separately permitted by God. But the opposite absolute also outruns the evidence.</p><p><a class="button" href="/truth/case-000001.php">Read Investigation</a></p></article><article class="card"><div class="case-head"><div><div class="case-id">TW-CLAIM-000002</div><h2>Did Jesus teach the modern Romans Road / sinner's prayer?</h2></div><div class="status">OPEN</div></div><p>A familiar evangelical salvation formula goes on trial against Jesus' recorded teaching, Romans itself, conversion history, and its strongest defense.</p><p><a class="button" href="/truth/case-000002.php">Examine Case</a></p></article></div></div></section><section class="section" id="ask"><div class="wrap grid"><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">YOUR TURN</div><h2>What do you think you know?</h2><p>Submit a question privately. Truth on Trial clarifies the actual claim, traces the source behind the source, actively seeks contrary evidence, and distinguishes proof from inference, opinion and unknowns.</p><form class="challenge" action="/truth/question-submit.php" method="post"><input type="hidden" name="opened_at" id="questionOpenedAt" value=""><div class="hp" aria-hidden="true"><label>Website<input name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label></div><label for="question">Put a claim or question on trial</label><textarea id="question" name="question" minlength="20" maxlength="3000" required placeholder="Ask something you think you know..."></textarea><label for="questionEmail">Email for an update (optional)</label><input id="questionEmail" type="email" name="email" maxlength="190" autocomplete="email"><input type="hidden" name="topic" value="other"><button class="button" type="submit">Put It on Trial</button></form></article><aside class="card"><div class="eyebrow">THE TRUST-WORTHY METHOD</div><h2>No protected conclusions.</h2><ul class="rules"><li>Trace toward primary and earliest accessible evidence.</li><li>Seek the strongest credible counterevidence.</li><li>Separate independent corroboration from repetition.</li><li>Examine motive, money and power without pretending motive is proof.</li><li>Label fact, inference, uncertainty and opinion distinctly.</li><li>Revise the finding when better evidence wins.</li></ul><div class="bobinated"><div class="eyebrow">Bobinated Opinion</div><p>When useful, we give a clearly labeled reasoned opinion based on the total pattern—and show exactly why.</p></div><div class="judge">YOU BE THE JUDGE.<small>POWERED BY TRUST-WORTHY</small></div></aside></div></section></main><footer class="footer"><div class="wrap"><strong>PROJECT UNVEILED</strong> · Truth on Trial · Powered by Trust-Worthy · <strong>YOU BE THE JUDGE.</strong></div></footer><script>document.getElementById("questionOpenedAt").value=Math.floor(Date.now()/1000);</script></body></html>